implementationPlan.description:
Implement in packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/getCommitScope.ts.
(a) Add `import { finalizingAttemptsByTask } from '../util/claimEligibility.js';` after the attemptStore import. Reuse it as-is: do not copy isHoldingFinalizingAttempt and do not edit claimEligibility.ts. Its predicate is the field's contract:
- phase 'finalizing';
- non-blank id, taskId and workerId;
- Number.isSafeInteger(generation) && generation >= 1;
- the highest generation wins, because listAttempts sorts by generation.
(b) Next to `const assigneeProtected = isAssigneeProtected(state, task);`, add:
```ts
      // The finalizing hold claim_next_task enforces (util/claimEligibility.ts), named whoever
      // holds it: the wrapper's owner guard compares workerId instead of parsing .moe/attempts.
      const finalizing = finalizingAttemptsByTask(state).get(task.id);
```
(c) In the returned object, right after `assigneeProtected,`, add:
```ts
        // Additive: an older daemon omits it, and the wrapper then scans .moe/attempts itself.
        finalizingAttempt: finalizing
          ? { attemptId: finalizing.id, workerId: finalizing.workerId, generation: finalizing.generation }
          : null,
```
Only these three properties. Never spread the attempt: runnerId, workspace and the timestamps stay off the wire.
(d) Append one sentence to the tool's `description` string, after '...must leave the task\'s source paths alone.':
' finalizingAttempt names the task\'s finalizing attempt exactly as claim_next_task\'s finalizing hold selects it ({attemptId, workerId, generation}, whoever holds it, the caller included) or is null; a daemon older than the field omits it.'

Error handling: finalizingAttemptsByTask skips malformed records instead of throwing (loadEntities admits any JSON with an id), so no new error path exists. The tool still never refuses a caller.
Cost: one in-memory pass over state.attempts per call, the same index claim_next_task builds per claim. get_commit_scope runs a few times per session.
